# "Ketramose can't attack or block unless there are seven or more cards in exile." With no card in exile, Bot1's Ketramose
# (on the battlefield since turn 1) is refused as an attacker on turn 3 and as a blocker of Bot2's attacking Ornithopter on turn
# 4, while Bot1's own Ornithopter (the creature that keeps the engine asking about attackers, and the positive control for the
# block) blocks without trouble. The positive controls for Ketramose itself (seven cards in exile) are in
# the other ketramose-* scenarios.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Ketramose, the New Dawn
Ornithopter
Island x2
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x26

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Ketramose, the New Dawn.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Attack(Ketramose, the New Dawn > Bot2)
Bot1.Attack()
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
! Bot1.Block(Ketramose, the New Dawn > Ornithopter)
Bot1.Block(Ornithopter > Ornithopter)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Ketramose, the New Dawn.Damage = 0
